        "original_id": "9c64978a-06dc-5aa1-bb45-c1c0dd1681f6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Luther, John Frederick of Saxony\n- Symbols: Luther seal, Luther rose\n- Places: Coburg Fortress, Augsburg\n- Events: Diet of Augsburg, Protestant Reformation\n- Topics: Lutheranism\n\nFacts:\n- Martin Luther was born on 10 November 1483 and died on 18 February 1546.\n- Martin Luther was a German professor of theology, composer, priest, monk, and a seminal figure in the Protestant Reformation.\n- In 1530, John Frederick of Saxony had the Luther seal designed for Martin Luther while Martin Luther was staying at the Coburg Fortress during the Diet of Augsburg.\n- The Luther seal, also called the Luther rose, is a widely recognized symbol of Lutheranism.",
